---
import BaseLayout from '../layouts/BaseLayout.astro';
import FaqItem from '../components/FaqItem.astro';
import MediaSlot from '../components/MediaSlot.astro';
import CtaBand from '../components/CtaBand.astro';
import { faqs, faqJsonLd } from '../data/faqs.js';

const experienceLines = [
  'You learn on real drums.',
  'You develop real skills.',
  'You play with other drummers.',
  'You get opportunities to perform.',
  'You become part of a community.',
];
---

<BaseLayout
  title="About & FAQ"
  description="Since 2005, Drum Sync Academy has been a 100% drums-only studio built around drum education and the drumming experience. Meet owner Kyle Schweikhard and get answers to common questions."
  jsonLd={faqJsonLd}
>
  <section class="border-b border-border bg-surface">
    <div class="mx-auto max-w-6xl px-4 py-20 sm:px-6">
      <h1 class="text-4xl font-bold uppercase text-white sm:text-5xl">About &amp; FAQ</h1>
      <p class="mt-5 max-w-2xl text-lg text-gray-light">
        Our story, our mission, the person behind DSA, and the questions we hear most.
      </p>
      <nav aria-label="On this page" class="mt-8">
        <ul class="flex flex-wrap gap-2 text-sm">
          {
            [
              ['Our Story', '#story'],
              ['Our Mission', '#mission'],
              ['Meet the Owner', '#owner'],
              ['FAQs', '#faq'],
            ].map(([l, h]) => (
              <li>
                <a href={h} class="inline-block rounded-full border border-border px-4 py-2 font-medium text-gray-light hover:border-red hover:text-white">
                  {l}
                </a>
              </li>
            ))
          }
        </ul>
      </nav>
    </div>
  </section>

  <!-- Our Story -->
  <section id="story" class="scroll-mt-24" aria-labelledby="story-title">
    <div class="mx-auto grid max-w-6xl gap-12 px-4 py-20 sm:px-6 lg:grid-cols-2 lg:items-start">
      <div>
        <p class="text-sm font-semibold uppercase tracking-wide text-red">Our Story</p>
        <h2 id="story-title" class="mt-2 text-3xl font-bold text-white sm:text-4xl">
          Built for drummers. Built around the experience.
        </h2>
        <div class="mt-6 space-y-5 text-lg leading-relaxed text-gray-light">
          <p>
            Since 2005, Drum Sync Academy has been creating a place where people
            can do more than simply take drum lessons.
          </p>
          <p>
            What started with a passion for drums and drum education has grown
            into a 100% drums-only studio where drummers can learn, play, grow,
            connect, and experience what it really means to be a drummer.
          </p>
          <p>At DSA, we believe the experience should go beyond the lesson room.</p>
          <ul class="space-y-1 border-l-2 border-red pl-5 font-display text-white">
            {experienceLines.map((l) => <li>{l}</li>)}
          </ul>
          <p>That’s what we mean when we say DSA is more than drum lessons.</p>
          <p>
            Over the years, DSA has continued to grow through classes, private
            instruction, programs, clinics, performances, and countless hours
            spent helping drummers develop their skills. But at the heart of it
            all, the idea has stayed the same:
          </p>
          <p class="text-xl font-semibold text-white">
            Create a place where people can learn the drums, enjoy the process,
            and keep growing as drummers.
          </p>
        </div>
      </div>
      <div class="grid grid-cols-2 gap-4 lg:sticky lg:top-28">
        {/* Reuses homepage photos. Swap in a true studio-interior wide shot or an
            archival early-years photo here if DSA has them. */}
        <MediaSlot
          src="/dsa-community-stage.jpg"
          alt="DSA drummers, teens and adults, holding drumsticks on the studio stage under the DSA sign"
          aspect="4/3"
          position="center top"
          class="col-span-2"
        />
        <MediaSlot
          src="/dsa-kids-and-families.jpg"
          alt="Kids, parents, and DSA instructors holding up drumsticks on the studio stage"
          aspect="1/1"
        />
        <MediaSlot
          src="/dsa-live-performance-outdoor.jpg"
          alt="A drummer grinning at the camera while playing a white drum kit on an outdoor stage"
          aspect="1/1"
          position="center top"
        />
      </div>
    </div>
  </section>

  <!-- Our Mission -->
  <section id="mission" class="scroll-mt-24 border-y border-border bg-surface" aria-labelledby="mission-title">
    <div class="mx-auto max-w-4xl px-4 py-20 sm:px-6">
      <p class="text-sm font-semibold uppercase tracking-wide text-red">Our Mission</p>
      <h2 id="mission-title" class="mt-2 text-3xl font-bold text-white sm:text-4xl">
        More than lessons. A real drum education.
      </h2>
      <div class="mt-6 space-y-5 text-lg leading-relaxed text-gray-light">
        <p class="text-xl text-white">
          Our mission is simple: provide a great drum education and create a
          great drumming experience.
        </p>
        <p>
          We believe learning the drums should be about more than learning a beat
          or playing a song. It’s about developing strong fundamentals,
          understanding the instrument, building confidence, discovering your
          musicality, and having opportunities to put those skills into action.
        </p>
        <p>
          That means giving drummers a structured path to learn while creating
          an environment where they can explore, have fun, perform, and connect
          with other people who love drums.
        </p>
        <p>
          Whether someone is picking up sticks for the first time or continuing
          a lifelong relationship with the instrument, we want them to have the
          tools, guidance, and environment to keep moving forward.
        </p>
      </div>
      <p class="mt-10 font-display text-2xl font-bold uppercase text-white sm:text-3xl">
        Learn. Play. Experience. Grow.
      </p>
      <p class="mt-2 text-lg text-red">That’s the DSA way.</p>
    </div>
  </section>

  <!-- Meet the Owner -->
  <section id="owner" class="scroll-mt-24" aria-labelledby="owner-title">
    <div class="mx-auto grid max-w-6xl gap-12 px-4 py-20 sm:px-6 lg:grid-cols-[minmax(0,2fr)_minmax(0,3fr)] lg:items-start">
      <div class="space-y-6 lg:sticky lg:top-28">
        {/* TODO(DSA-media): portrait of Kyle Schweikhard, ideally at the kit in the studio (3:4). */}
        <MediaSlot alt="Kyle Schweikhard, owner and founder of Drum Sync Academy" label="Kyle Schweikhard" aspect="3/4" />
        {/* TODO(DSA-media): optional "Welcome from Kyle" video (30–60s), talking to camera
            about DSA's philosophy. Pass src + poster to fill; delete this slot if unused. */}
        <div>
          <MediaSlot type="video" alt="Video: a welcome from Kyle" label="Welcome from Kyle" aspect="16/9" />
          <p class="mt-2 text-sm text-gray-muted">A welcome from Kyle</p>
        </div>
      </div>

      <div>
        <p class="text-sm font-semibold uppercase tracking-wide text-red">Meet the Owner</p>
        <h2 id="owner-title" class="mt-2 text-3xl font-bold text-white sm:text-4xl">Kyle Schweikhard</h2>
        <p class="mt-2 font-display text-lg text-gray-light">Drummer. Educator. Clinician. Entrepreneur.</p>
        <div class="mt-6 space-y-5 text-lg leading-relaxed text-gray-light">
          <p>At the heart of Drum Sync Academy is its owner and founder, Kyle Schweikhard.</p>
          <p>
            A professional drummer, educator, clinician, and entrepreneur, Kyle
            created DSA in 2005 with a vision for something more than a
            traditional drum lesson studio.
          </p>
          <p>His philosophy is simple:</p>
          <blockquote class="border-l-2 border-red pl-5 font-display text-2xl font-semibold text-white">
            “DSA provides not just drum lessons, but a drum education.”
          </blockquote>
          <p>That philosophy has shaped DSA from the beginning.</p>
          <p>
            Kyle’s passion for drums extends beyond playing the instrument. He
            believes in understanding how and why we play, developing strong
            fundamentals, creating meaningful opportunities for drummers, and
            building an environment where people can genuinely enjoy being
            around the instrument.
          </p>
          <p>
            That vision is what helped shape DSA into a 100% drums-only
            community—a place built specifically around the education,
            experience, and culture of drumming.
          </p>
          <p>From the lesson room to the stage, the goal has always been the same:</p>
          <p class="text-white">
            Help people become better drummers, give them something to be
            excited about, and create a place they’re happy to be part of.
          </p>
          <p>And after all these years, there’s still one thing that hasn’t changed:</p>
          <p class="font-display text-2xl font-bold text-white">We really, really love drums.</p>
        </div>
      </div>
    </div>
  </section>

  <!-- FAQ -->
  <section id="faq" class="scroll-mt-24 border-t border-border bg-surface" aria-labelledby="faq-title">
    <div class="mx-auto max-w-3xl px-4 py-20 sm:px-6">
      <h2 id="faq-title" class="text-3xl font-bold uppercase text-white sm:text-4xl">FAQs</h2>
      <div class="mt-8 space-y-3">
        {
          faqs.map((f) => (
            <FaqItem question={f.q}>
              <Fragment set:html={f.a} />
            </FaqItem>
          ))
        }
      </div>
    </div>
  </section>

  <CtaBand
    heading="Ready to Experience DSA?"
    body="All new DSA drummers begin with a Studio Tour. No pressure, no commitment—just a chance to see if we’re a good fit."
    label="Request a Studio Tour"
  />
</BaseLayout>
